WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.136
Hi, I'm Mabel!

00:00:02.136 --> 00:00:05.803
Video models get sped up over and over, once for every new version.

00:00:05.803 --> 00:00:09.751
Here is a way to do that work a single time, and reuse it.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:15.301
Learn a speedup once as a small adapter on a base model,

00:00:15.301 --> 00:00:19.581
then plug that same adapter into its many downstream descendants without any retraining.

00:00:21.717 --> 00:00:25.051
First, learn the speedup once on a frozen base model.

00:00:25.051 --> 00:00:27.051
It becomes a small, reusable adapter.

00:00:27.471 --> 00:00:31.684
Snap that same adapter onto a whole family of models built from that base.

00:00:31.684 --> 00:00:32.586
No new training.

00:00:33.006 --> 00:00:34.791
Then onto two more families.

00:00:34.791 --> 00:00:38.716
One adapter, dozens of downstream models, each keeping its own weights.

00:00:40.192 --> 00:00:43.403
The usual way trains a new speedup into every model.

00:00:43.403 --> 00:00:45.973
Fresh data and a teacher, every single time.

00:00:46.393 --> 00:00:48.996
Here, one adapter is learned once and plugged in.

00:00:48.996 --> 00:00:51.600
The bill stays flat as the models pile up.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.512
On one world model, plain four-step video is blurry.

00:00:56.512 --> 00:01:00.438
The reused adapter scores far better, almost matching a model trained

00:01:00.438 --> 00:01:01.865
only for that task.

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:04.625
And the cost?

00:01:04.625 --> 00:01:09.642
One family's whole speedup runs about eighty cluster-hours, however many models reuse it.

00:01:09.642 --> 00:01:12.344
Re-training each instead runs past four hundred.

00:01:13.725 --> 00:01:17.971
Distillation stops being baked into one model and becomes an adapter you

00:01:17.971 --> 00:01:20.802
train once and carry to every compatible descendant.

00:01:22.192 --> 00:01:26.317
To recap: distill once on a base, plug the adapter into compatible

00:01:26.317 --> 00:01:29.411
models, and stop paying for distillation again and again.

00:01:29.831 --> 00:01:31.923
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:31.923 --> 00:01:32.521
I'm Mabel.

00:01:32.521 --> 00:01:32.820
Bye!
